{"type":"message","id":"5e4dcff2","parentId":"bf3c597f","timestamp":"2026-06-03T00:13:52.337Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I have a clear picture. Let me lay out the plan.\n\nFiles to modify:\n1. `crypto_signal_monitor.py` - the main file\n   - `calc_tp_sl()` function: change SL from fixed -2% entry to ATR-dynamic + current-price-protected\n   - The SL trigger section in main loop: fix to not delete local position if close failed\n\n2. `auto_trade_config.json` - might need to update SL config comments/parameters\n\nThe key changes:\n\n**calc_tp_sl()** - need to access ATR data. It currently receives `ind` (indicators) and `price_data`. Let me check what's in `price_data` — it should have ATR.\n\nActually, looking at the function signature: `calc_tp_sl(entry, direction, ind, price_data)`. The `price_data` should contain ATR. But I need to check how this function is called to understand what kind of ATR data is available.\n\nLet me also look at where `calc_tp_sl` is called to understand the timing — is it only called at position open, or throughout the lifecycle?\n\nActually, the important fix is for the lifecycle management. When a position is already open and in drawdown >2%, the bot tries to sync SL to Binance via `sync_stop_loss_to_binance` and `submit_initial_algo_orders`. Both use the `pos[\"sl_price\"]` which was set by `calc_tp_sl` at open time.\n\nBut `calc_tp_sl` only runs at position open time. The fix should be in how the SL is continuously re-evaluated, not just at open time.\n\nActually, there are two places to fix:\n\n1. `calc_tp_sl()` - for NEW positions, use ATR-based SL from the start. This prevents positions from having too-tight SL in the first place.\n\n2. The `submit_initial_algo_orders()` and `sync_stop_loss_to_binance()` functions - when they submit an Algo stop order, they should check if the SL price is valid (not \"immediately triggering\"). If it would trigger, they should compute a fallback SL based on current price.\n\nBut actually, the simplest and most effective fix is in `compute_tp_sl`/`calc_tp_sl` to make SL wider using ATR. And then the secondary fix is in the main loop where SL-triggered close might fail.\n\nWait, I think the key insight is: the SL doesn't need to be \"protected from current price\" at calculation time. The SL just needs to be WIDE ENOUGH that when calculated from entry, it won't be immediately breached by normal market moves. Using ATR * multiplier for SL distance instead of a flat 2% should fix most cases.\n\nLet me look at what ATR period the price_stream reports, and what data is available in calc_tp_sl.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_b4lIXCxCIsAPQfH05qMk4521","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n 'calc_tp_sl\\|compute_tp_sl' ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py | head -20","timeout":10}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_Q8ptgwAIOLJgs9zChbLc0389","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -A15 'class PriceStream\\|def get(self\\|\"atr\"\\|ATR' ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py | head -40","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":250,"output":1441,"cacheRead":38272,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":39963,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780445616345}}
