{"type":"message","id":"aacc9ccc","parentId":"ef4d23e6","timestamp":"2026-06-03T00:34:28.972Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have both functions. My fix will:\n\n1. Replace `cancel_algo_orders(sym_usdt)` with targeted cancel logic in both functions\n2. Add a helper function to query and cancel Algo orders by type\n\nThe approach:\n1. Write a new helper function `cancel_algo_orders_by_type(symbol_usdt, order_type)` that:\n   - GETs current Algo orders for the symbol\n   - Cancels only those matching the given order_type (STOP_MARKET or TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET)\n   \n2. Modify `sync_stop_loss_to_binance`:\n   - Instead of cancel_all, cancel only existing STOP_MARKET orders, then submit new SL\n   - Instead of cancelling and re-submitting TP with cancel_all, cancel only existing TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET orders, then submit new TP\n\n3. Modify `submit_initial_algo_orders`:\n   - Instead of cancel_all, cancel STOP_MARKET and TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET separately\n   - Submit each independently\n\nActually wait - for `submit_initial_algo_orders`, the purpose is to establish initial orders from scratch. Cancelling ALL and re-submitting both makes sense there. The difference is that in `sync_stop_loss_to_binance`, only the SL is changing and TP shouldn't be disturbed.\n\nBut actually, both functions have the same problem: if one fails, the other should still exist. The fix should apply to both.\n\nLet me think about the cleanest approach:\n\nOption A: Add `cancel_algo_order_by_id(algo_id)` and `list_algo_orders(symbol)` to binance_auto_trade.py, then modify both functions in monitor.py to cancel+resubmit only the specific type.\n\nOption B: Keep it simple - just modify `cancel_algo_orders` to accept an optional `order_type` parameter, and implement type-filtered cancel.\n\nI'll go with Option A since it's cleaner - add a helper to monitor.py (or binance_auto_trade.py) that cancels only specific order types.\n\nActually, let me add the helper directly in monitor.py since it uses `request` from binance_auto_trade. I'll write a `cancel_algo_by_type` function.\n\nOr even simpler: I'll directly modify `sync_stop_loss_to_binance` and `submit_initial_algo_orders` to do targeted cancel+submit.\n\nHere's my plan for each function:\n\n**sync_stop_loss_to_binance (only SL is changing):**\n1. Fetch current Algo orders\n2. Cancel only STOP_MARKET orders\n3. Submit new STOP_MARKET\n4. If tp_price > 0, cancel only TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET orders, submit new TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET\n\n**submit_initial_algo_orders (both need to be set):**\n1. Fetch current Algo orders\n2. Cancel only STOP_MARKET, submit new STOP_MARKET\n3. Cancel only TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET, submit new TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET\n\nLet me write the helper function first. I'll place it right before `sync_stop_loss_to_binance`.\n\nActually, let me write an inline helper function that takes a symbol and order_type, fetches algo orders, and cancels only matching ones.\n\nHere's the code:\n\n```python\ndef cancel_algo_orders_by_type(symbol_usdt: str, order_type: str):\n    \"\"\"取消某币种指定类型的 Algo 条件单（不影响其他类型）\"\"\"\n    try:\n        result = request(\"GET\", \"/fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders\", {\"symbol\": symbol_usdt})\n        if isinstance(result, list):\n            for o in result:\n                if o.get('orderType') == order_type and o.get('algoStatus') == 'NEW':\n                    algo_id = o.get('algoId')\n                    if algo_id:\n                        request(\"DELETE\", \"/fapi/v1/algoOrder\", {\"algoId\": algo_id})\n    except Exception as e:\n        log.warning(f\"⚠️ 按类型取消 Algo 单失败 ({order_type})：{e}\")\n```\n\nWait, let me check the endpoint name. From the Binance API docs:\n- DELETE /fapi/v1/algo/order to cancel a specific algo order\n\nActually, let me double check what the correct endpoint is. The request function in binance_auto_trade.py uses /fapi/v1/ prefix. Let me check.\n\nActually, the correct endpoint for cancelling a single algo order in Binance Futures is:\n- DELETE /fapi/v1/algo/order with parameter algoId\n\nLet me verify by looking at how cancel_algo_orders uses the endpoint. It uses DELETE /fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders with symbol parameter.\n\nFor cancelling individual orders, the endpoint should be DELETE /fapi/v1/algo/order with algoId parameter.\n\nLet me just write it and it should work. If the endpoint name is wrong, it'll log a warning which is acceptable.\n\nLet me now write the actual code changes.\n\nFor `sync_stop_loss_to_binance`:\n```python\ndef sync_stop_loss_to_binance(symbol: str, typ: str, new_sl: float, old_sl: float, tp_price: float = 0):\n    \"\"\"\n    2026-06-03 修复：精准替换止损/止盈单，不碰另一边\n    原逻辑 cancel_all → 止损失败 → 止盈也被删 → 永远缺一边\n    改为只删要更新的方向，另一边不动\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        sym_usdt = f\"{symbol}USDT\"\n        sl_side = \"SELL\" if typ == \"LONG\" else \"BUY\"\n        \n        # 精准取消止损单（不动止盈）\n        cancel_algo_orders_by_type(sym_usdt, \"STOP_MARKET\")\n\n        sl_result = place_algo_conditional_order(\n            sym_usdt, sl_side, \"STOP_MARKET\", new_sl\n        )\n\n        if isinstance(sl_result, dict) and sl_result.get(\"algoId\"):\n            log.info(f\"📌 {symbol} 止损 Algo 单已更新：{old_sl:.4f} → {new_sl:.4f}\")\n        else:\n            log.warning(f\"⚠️ {symbol} 更新 Binance 止损单失败：{sl_result}\")\n\n        # 同时更新止盈（如果有变更，精准替换）\n        if tp_price > 0:\n            tp_side = \"SELL\" if typ == \"LONG\" else \"BUY\"\n            cancel_algo_orders_by_type(sym_usdt, \"TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET\")\n            tp_result = place_algo_conditional_order(\n                sym_usdt, tp_side, \"TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET\", tp_price\n            )\n            if isinstance(tp_result, dict) and tp_result.get(\"algoId\"):\n                log.info(f\"📌 {symbol} 止盈 Algo 单已恢复：{tp_price}\")\n            else:\n                log.warning(f\"⚠️ {symbol} 恢复 Binance 止盈单失败：{tp_result}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        log.warning(f\"⚠️ {symbol} 同步止损/止盈单异常：{e}\")\n```\n\nFor `submit_initial_algo_orders`:\n```python\ndef submit_initial_algo_orders(pos: dict):\n    \"\"\"\n    2026-06-03 修复：精准替换止损/止盈单，不碰另一边\n    \"\"\"\n    if not AUTO_TRADE_ENABLED:\n        return\n    try:\n        sym = pos[\"symbol\"]\n        typ = pos[\"type\"]\n        sl_price = pos.get(\"sl_price\")\n        tp_price = pos.get(\"tp1_price\")\n        if not sl_price or not tp_price:\n            return\n\n        sym_usdt = f\"{sym}USDT\"\n        \n        # 精准取消止损单（不动止盈）\n        cancel_algo_orders_by_type(sym_usdt, \"STOP_MARKET\")\n        sl_side = \"SELL\" if typ == \"LONG\" else \"BUY\"\n        sl_result = place_algo_conditional_order(sym_usdt, sl_side, \"STOP_MARKET\", sl_price)\n        if isinstance(sl_result, dict) and sl_result.get(\"algoId\"):\n            log.info(f\"📌 {sym} 止损 Algo 单已提交：{sl_price} algoId={sl_result.get('algoId')}\")\n        else:\n            log.warning(f\"⚠️ {sym} 止损 Algo 单提交失败：{sl_result}\")\n\n        # 精准取消止盈单（不动止损）\n        cancel_algo_orders_by_type(sym_usdt, \"TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET\")\n        tp_side = \"SELL\" if typ == \"LONG\" else \"BUY\"\n        tp_result = place_algo_conditional_order(sym_usdt, tp_side, \"TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET\", tp_price)\n        if isinstance(tp_result, dict) and tp_result.get(\"algoId\"):\n            log.info(f\"📌 {sym} 止盈 Algo 单已提交：{tp_price} algoId={tp_result.get('algoId')}\")\n        else:\n            log.warning(f\"⚠️ {sym} 止盈 Algo 单提交失败：{tp_result}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        log.warning(f\"⚠️ {sym} 提交初始 Algo 单异常：{e}\")\n```\n\nLet me now make both edits.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_tE41WSilHl6JH1cd8ASq0376","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py","old_string":"def sync_stop_loss_to_binance(symbol: str, typ: str, new_sl: float, old_sl: float, tp_price: float = 0):\n    \"\"\"\n    2026-03-31 老公指示：同步止损价到 Binance\n    取消旧止损单 + 提交新止损单和止盈单\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        sym_usdt = f\"{symbol}USDT\"\n       