{"type":"message","id":"2e1e8664","parentId":"7ec14594","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:18:47.609Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, there are only 3 positions in the local file (LINK, DOT, ETH) but 4 on Binance. XRP is missing! The monitor restarted and only loaded 3 of the 4 API positions into the local file.\n\nAlso, I can see the `qty` field IS present now (21.23, 11.7, 0.008), matching the `amount` field. So `pos.get(\"qty\", 0)` should return the correct value.\n\nBut wait, XRP is missing from the local file! Let me check if it was there and the file is incomplete, or if the monitor didn't properly sync all 4 positions.\n\nLooking at the Binance data:\n- DOT: 11.7, XRP: -139.8, ETH: 0.008, LINK: 21.23\n\nAnd the local file has DOT, ETH, LINK but not XRP. That's a problem.\n\nBut the main issue is the ReduceOnly rejection. Let me think about this...\n\nActually, wait — maybe XRP was already removed from local because its SL triggered and position was closed? Let me check the logs for XRP.\n\nActually, the query_positions output at 11:17:12 showed all 4 positions including XRP. But the local file only has 3. That means query_positions reads from Binance API, not from the local file.\n\nOK, let me focus on the ReduceOnly issue. The quantities look correct:\n- DOT: 11.7 (matches Binance)\n- ETH: 0.008 (matches Binance)\n- LINK: 21.23 (matches Binance)\n\nSo the quantity isn't the issue. Something else is wrong.\n\nLet me look at the entire place_order flow for a close:\n```python\norder_params = {\n    \"symbol\": symbol,       # \"ETHUSDT\"\n    \"side\": \"SELL\",         # LONG position → SELL\n    \"type\": \"MARKET\",\n    \"quantity\": 0.008,      # formatted quantity\n    \"reduceOnly\": \"true\"\n}\norder_result = request(\"POST\", \"/fapi/v1/order\", order_params)\n```\n\nThis should work. MARKET SELL 0.008 ETH with reduceOnly=true to close a 0.008 ETH LONG position.\n\nUnless... the side is wrong. Wait, let me check: the positions from Binance API show `positionSide: \"BOTH\"` which means ONE_WAY mode. In ONE_WAY mode:\n- Long position: positive positionAmt\n- To close: SELL order, reduceOnly=true\n- This should work\n\nLet me think of other possibilities...\n\nActually, maybe the issue is specific to Binance Testnet. Sometimes Testnet has weird behavior. Or maybe there's an ongoing position already being closed by a pending order.\n\nWait, let me check if there are any open orders (not Algo orders).","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_XJIGhE9AS3WbwtogRpNn4762","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request\n# Check regular open orders\nresult = request('GET', '/fapi/v1/openOrders')\nif isinstance(result, list):\n    if len(result) == 0:\n        print('无普通挂单')\n    else:\n        for o in result:\n            print(json.dumps(o, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\nelse:\n    print(json.dumps(result, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":284,"output":1418,"cacheRead":85888,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":87590,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780456711436}}
