{"type":"message","id":"6cd6e6a0","parentId":"06fbab0b","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:19:30.407Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even a direct manual close gets -2022. This is a fundamental Binance API issue, not a code bug. Let me investigate why.\n\nPossible reasons for -2022 \"ReduceOnly Order is rejected\" even when the position exists:\n1. The position quantity doesn't match what we're trying to close\n2. The position side doesn't match the order side\n3. The account has issues on testnet\n4. There's some Binance Testnet-specific behavior\n\nLet me check if there are any position-related issues. The ETH position has positionAmt=0.008, which is a LONG position. A SELL MARKET order with reduceOnly=true and quantity=0.008 should close it.\n\nWait - maybe the issue is that we already submitted an Algo order (STOP_MARKET or TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET) that's blocking new orders? In Binance Futures, having an open Algo order for the same position shouldn't block regular orders...\n\nActually, let me check something else. The Algo orders from the first check had `closePosition: true`. If there's an open Algo STOP_MARKET or TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET with `closePosition: true`, and the order is in NEW status, maybe Binance is reserving the position for that Algo order?\n\nLet me check this theory by canceling all Algo orders and trying to close again.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_shC8FfV56UfCVMeqw3Yc4588","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request, format_quantity\n\n# Cancel all Algo orders first\nresult = request('DELETE', '/fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders', {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT'})\nprint(f'Cancel ETH algo: {result}')\n\nresult = request('DELETE', '/fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders', {'symbol': 'DOTUSDT'})\nprint(f'Cancel DOT algo: {result}')\n\nresult = request('DELETE', '/fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders', {'symbol': 'LINKUSDT'})\nprint(f'Cancel LINK algo: {result}')\n\nresult = request('DELETE', '/fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders', {'symbol': 'XRPUSDT'})\nprint(f'Cancel XRP algo: {result}')\n\n# Now try to close ETH\nimport time\ntime.sleep(0.5)\n\nsymbol = 'ETHUSDT'\nquantity = format_quantity('ETH', 0.008, 1849)\nparams = {\n    'symbol': symbol,\n    'side': 'SELL',\n    'type': 'MARKET',\n    'quantity': quantity,\n    'reduceOnly': 'true',\n}\nresult = request('POST', '/fapi/v1/order', params)\nprint(f'ETH close result: {json.dumps(result, indent=2)}' if isinstance(result, dict) else str(result))\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":111,"output":973,"cacheRead":87808,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":88892,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780456756614}}
