{"type":"message","id":"504e84b1","parentId":"fec69e42","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:31:35.796Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"LIMIT reduceOnly also fails. So reduceOnly is completely broken on this Binance testnet for all order types.\n\nThe only working approach for ETH (notional < $20) is:\n1. INCREASE the position first to make notional ≥ $20 (buy more ETH, bringing total to ≥ 0.011 ETH)\n2. Then close the whole thing without reduceOnly\n\nBut this is risky because we're adding to a losing position just to close it.\n\nAlternatively, try the new Binance endpoint: POST /fapi/v1/order with `positionSide` parameter.\n\nWait actually, let me try something else: close the position by opening an opposite position of the SAME SIZE but with a SELL. Since 0.008 * 1849 = $14.79 < $20, we can't open a new 0.008 short. But we could BUY additional ETH to bring the notional up, then sell all.\n\nActually, the simplest approach: add 0.003 more ETH (0.003 * $1849 = $5.55), bringing total to 0.011 ETH (0.011 * $1849 = $20.34 ≥ $20). Then SELL 0.011 without reduceOnly.\n\nOr even simpler: since this is only a testnet issue, I can modify the code to handle the -4164/minimum notional case by:\n1. If -4164 and position notional < $20: BUY additional to reach $20 notional, then SELL all without reduceOnly\n2. This is a testnet-specific workaround\n\nBut wait, this is getting complex. The issue only affects ETH because it's the only position with notional < $20:\n- DOT was 11.7 * $1.08 = $12.69 — wait, DOT was $12.69 too! But my non-reduceOnly order for DOT succeeded?\n- Actually, DOT was already closed during the test. Let me think...\n\nActually, looking back at the test results:\n```\nDOTUSDT SELL MARKET (no reduceOnly): orderId=228557089, status=NEW\n```\nBut later DOT positionAmt=0.0. So the MARKET order for DOT DID fill, even though notional was $12.69. But the order was NOT reduceOnly — it was a regular MARKET SELL.\n\nWait, how did DOT work? DOT notional = 11.7 * $1.085 = $12.69 < $20. But the MARKET SELL without reduceOnly succeeded?\n\nLet me re-check. DOT was 11.7 DOT at ~$1.085. Notional = $12.69. If the minimum notional is $20 for non-reduceOnly... but it worked for DOT?\n\nOh wait, maybe the market price changed and brought DOT above $1.71 (11.7 * 1.71 = $20)? No, DOT was $1.085.\n\nOr maybe the minimum notional rule only applies to certain order creation paths... Let me actually test ETH differently. What if I just increase the position by buying a tiny amount, then close?","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_SyBkKi5Tnqdqxr1ZFX5t7917","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys, time\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request\n\nsym = 'ETHUSDT'\n# Step 1: Add a tiny BUY to boost notional above $20\n# Need total > 20/1849 = 0.0108 ETH. Have 0.008, need 0.003 more.\nprint('Buy 0.003 ETH...')\nr = request('POST', '/fapi/v1/order', {\n    'symbol': sym, 'side': 'BUY', 'type': 'MARKET',\n    'quantity': 0.003\n})\nprint(json.dumps(r, indent=2) if isinstance(r, dict) else r)\n\ntime.sleep(1)\n# Check position\nr = request('GET', '/fapi/v2/positionRisk', {'symbol': sym})\namt = float(r[0]['positionAmt']) if isinstance(r, list) else 0\nprint(f'ETH AFTER BUY: positionAmt={amt}')\n\nif amt > 0:\n    print(f'Selling {amt} ETH...')\n    r = request('POST', '/fapi/v1/order', {\n        'symbol': sym, 'side': 'SELL', 'type': 'MARKET',\n        'quantity': amt\n    })\n    print(json.dumps(r, indent=2) if isinstance(r, dict) else r)\n    \n    time.sleep(1)\n    r = request('GET', '/fapi/v2/positionRisk', {'symbol': sym})\n    amt2 = float(r[0]['positionAmt']) if isinstance(r, list) else 0\n    print(f'ETH FINAL: positionAmt={amt2}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":20}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":278,"output":1762,"cacheRead":106240,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":108280,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780457472841}}
