{"type":"message","id":"f75fb614","parentId":"74e11b81","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:50:27.414Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_9HZ90bZafxtb4LUxKF6h3443","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"def kv_block(items: list, columns: int = 2) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    生成 key-value 网格区块（飞书原生 div 的 fields 字段）\n    \n    items: [(label, value), ...]\n    columns: 每行几列（飞书最多 2）\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"tag\": \"div\",\n        \"fields\": [\n            {\n                \"is_short\": True,\n                \"text\": {\"tag\": \"lark_md\", \"content\": f\"**{label}**\\n{value}\"},\n            }\n            for label, value in items\n        ],\n    }"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":79,"aggregated":"def kv_block(items: list, columns: int = 2) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    生成 key-value 网格区块（飞书原生 div 的 fields 字段）\n    \n    items: [(label, value), ...]\n    columns: 每行几列（飞书最多 2）\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"tag\": \"div\",\n        \"fields\": [\n            {\n                \"is_short\": True,\n                \"text\": {\"tag\": \"lark_md\", \"content\": f\"**{label}**\\n{value}\"},\n            }\n            for label, value in items\n        ],\n    }","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780458627407}}
{"type":"message","id":"0e333ad7","parentId":"f75fb614","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:50:41.806Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The kv_block looks correct - it generates a `div` with `fields` array, each field being short with lark_md content. This is a standard Feishu card format. It should work.\n\nThe issue might be that `md()` returns a `div` too, but `note()` might use unsupported tags. Let me check `note()`.\n\nActually, wait - the issue could be the `content` field in the Feishu message. Let me try sending a test card directly to see if it renders properly.\n\nLet me also check the `_load_chat_id()` function to make sure it's pushing to the right chat.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The `[PUSH] OK` means the API call succeeded (code 0). The card was delivered but is showing blank. This could mean:\n1. The card format is valid but renders nothing\n2. The card has elements that Feishu rejects silently\n3. The nest of elements is wrong\n\nLet me test the exact card payload by sending it directly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_1JoYFDfTq5D2EzKSxpL97806","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport sys, json\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nfrom feishu_helper import get_token, _load_chat_id\n\nchat_id = _load_chat_id()\nprint(f'chat_id: {chat_id}')\ntoken = get_token()\nprint(f'token: {token[:20]}...')\n\ncard = {\n    'config': {'wide_screen_mode': True},\n    'header': {\n        'template': 'blue',\n        'title': {'tag': 'plain_text', 'content': '👑 测试行情'},\n    },\n    'elements': [\n        {\n            'tag': 'div',\n            'fields': [\n                {'is_short': True, 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': '**👑 BTC**\\n\\$65,771.8'}},\n                {'is_short': True, 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': '**💎 ETH**\\n\\$1,826.0'}},\n                {'is_short': True, 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': '**⚡ SOL**\\n\\$72.82'}},\n                {'is_short': True, 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': '**🔶 BNB**\\n\\$633.53'}},\n                {'is_short': True, 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': '**🌐 DOT**\\n\\$1.062'}},\n                {'is_short': True, 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': '**🔗 LINK**\\n\\$8.213'}},\n                {'is_short': True, 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': '**🪙 XRP**\\n\\$1.1958'}},\n                {'is_short': True, 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': ''}},\n            ]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\nimport requests\nurl = f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages?receive_id_type=chat_id'\nheaders = {'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'}\npayload = {\n    'receive_id': chat_id,\n    'msg_type': 'interactive',\n    'content': json.dumps(card, ensure_ascii=False),\n}\nr = requests.post(url, headers=headers, data=json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False), timeout=10, proxies=None)\ndata = r.json()\nprint(f'Response: code={data.get(\\\"code\\\")}, msg={data.get(\\\"msg\\\")}')\nif data.get('code') != 0:\n    print(f'Full: {json.dumps(data, indent=2)}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":268,"output":1127,"cacheRead":55040,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":56435,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780458627419}}
