{"type":"message","id":"ddb4bdd0","parentId":"f70b8189","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:51:23.488Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test card was sent successfully (code=0). If 老公 still sees blank cards, there might be a Feishu-side rendering issue with the `fields` + `lark_md` combination, or perhaps the card is being delivered but the format is causing issues.\n\nLet me also check if the original push_card function uses the right `content` format. Let me look at push_card more carefully...\n\nActually wait, let me re-read the push_card code:\n\n```python\npayload = {\n    \"receive_id\": chat_id,\n    \"msg_type\": \"interactive\",\n    \"content\": json.dumps(card_content, ensure_ascii=False),\n}\n```\n\nAnd the actual POST data is:\n```python\ndata=json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False),\n```\n\nSo the payload has `content` as a JSON string, and the whole payload is also a JSON string. That's double-encoding which is wrong!\n\nThe issue is: `card_content` is already a dict, then `json.dumps(card_content, ensure_ascii=False)` makes it a string. Then the whole `payload` dict is JSON-encoded again with `json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False)`.\n\nThis means `content` is a string inside a JSON string, which is correct for Feishu API (the content field should be a JSON string for interactive messages). Wait, let me check Feishu API docs...\n\nActually, the standard way is:\n```json\n{\n  \"receive_id\": \"oc_xxx\",\n  \"msg_type\": \"interactive\",\n  \"content\": \"{\\\"config\\\": {...}, \\\"header\\\": {...}}\"\n}\n```\n\nWhere `content` is a JSON-encoded string of the card. So the double-encoding is correct: `card_content` → `json.dumps` → string, then `payload` → `json.dumps` → HTTP body.\n\nBut wait, in my test I did the same thing and it worked with code=0. So the API call is fine.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the `\\` backslash characters in the price formatting are causing issues. In the `query_price.py`, the price is formatted as `f\"` ${px:,g}`\"` which generates backtick-enclosed prices. But in the lark_md content, backticks are used for inline code formatting.\n\nActually, looking at the price format again:\n```python\nitems.append((f\"{emo} {sym}\", f\"`${px:,g}`\"))\n```\n\nThis generates text like `` **👑 BTC**\\n`$65,771.8` ``. The backticks are for inline code formatting in lark_md. This should work.\n\nLet me actually try the exact same card that query_price.py builds, but with debug output to see the exact JSON.\n\nWait, actually , I already built and sent a test card and it returned code=0. Let me ask 老公 to check if he sees THAT card (the \"👑 测试行情\" one).\n\nBut actually, maybe I should just look at the actual issue more carefully. The first push was with `ALL` which failed. The second push was with `BTC ETH SOL BNB DOT LINK XRP --push` which succeeded. \n\nHmm, let me re-check: the first time I ran `python3 query_price.py ALL --push` and it said:\n```\n[OK] 实时价格 (更新于 3 秒前)\n  ALL: 不在监控列表\n```\nBut then `[PUSH] OK` was still printed. This means the push_card function was called but with an empty card (only \"未找到任何匹配币种\" message).\n\nThen the second time I ran `python3 query_price.py BTC ETH SOL BNB DOT LINK XRP --push` and got `[PUSH] OK`.\n\nBoth should have been delivered. Let me check if there's a timing issue or if Feishu is rejecting the cards for some reason.\n\nActually, let me just look at the problem from a different angle. The `push_card` function sends the message but maybe the `content` field in the response is the card, and the JSON encoding is correct. Let me verify by looking at the exact request sent.\n\nWait, I think I found it. Let me look at the push_card function again:\n\n```python\ndata=json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False),\n```\n\nAnd in `payload`:\n```python\npayload = {\n    \"receive_id\": chat_id,\n    \"msg_type\": \"interactive\",\n    \"content\": json.dumps(card_content, ensure_ascii=False),\n}\n```\n\nThe data being POSTed is `json.dumps(payload)`. Since `payload[\"content\"]` is already a JSON string, this means the HTTP body looks like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"receive_id\": \"oc_xxx\",\n  \"msg_type\": \"interactive\",\n  \"content\": \"{...card_content...}\"\n}\n```\n\nBut wait, in the `data` parameter of `requests.post`, when Content-Type is `application/json`, the `data` should be either:\n1. A dict (which requests will JSON-encode)\n2. A pre-encoded JSON string\n\nSince `data=json.dumps(payload, ...)`, it sends a JSON string. But wait, when `data` is a string and Content-Type is `application/json`, it sends the string as-is. This is correct.\n\nBut there's an issue: `payload[\"content\"]` is `json.dumps(card_content, ensure_ascii=False)`. And the whole payload is `json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False)`. So the `content` field in the final JSON would be double-encoded:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"receive_id\": \"oc_xxx\", \n  \"msg_type\": \"interactive\",\n  \"content\": \"{\\\"config\\\":{...},\\\"header\\\":{...}}\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is actually CORRECT for Feishu API - the `content` field should be a serialized JSON string.\n\nOK so the API call is correct. Let me just verify by checking with 老公 if the test card \"👑 测试行情\" appeared. If it did, the format is fine and the issue was just the ALL parameter.\n\nActually wait, I realize I should just check if the cards are really blank or if 老公 missed them. But since he said \"两次问你都是推送空白\", I need to investigate.\n\nLet me try one more thing: look at what the actual JSON payload looks like when query_price.py builds the card. Let me just run the query and capture the debug output.\n\nActually, let me just try sending with a simpler format to see if the issue persists with feishu_helper's push_card specifically.\n\nLet me just test a minimal card push.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Z7Ha2ogxH2DmRqUS4UBJ1612","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nfrom feishu_helper import get_token, _load_chat_id, md, note\nimport requests\n\nchat_id = _load_chat_id()\ntoken = get_token()\n\n# Simplest possible card\ncard = {\n    'config': {'wide_screen_mode': True},\n    'header': {\n        'template': 'blue',\n        'title': {'tag': 'plain_text', 'content': '🧪 极简测试'},\n    },\n    'elements': [\n        {'tag': 'div', 'text': {'tag': 'lark_md', 'content': 'BTC: **65,771.8** USDT\\nETH: **1,826.0** USDT'}},\n        {'tag': 'hr'},\n        {'tag': 'note', 'elements': [{'tag': 'plain_text', 'content': '📡 Binance · 11:49'}]},\n    ]\n}\n\nurl = f'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages?receive_id_type=chat_id'\npayload = {'receive_id': chat_id, 'msg_type': 'interactive', 'content': json.dumps(card, ensure_ascii=False)}\nr = requests.post(url,\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'},\n    data=json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False), timeout=10, proxies=None)\nprint(f'Minimal test: code={r.json().get(\\\"code\\\")}' )\n\n# Also test with kv_block (the format query_price uses)  \nfrom feishu_helper import kv_block\nitems = [('👑 BTC', '\\$65,771.8'), ('💎 ETH', '\\$1,826.0')]\ncard2 = {\n    'config': {'wide_screen_mode': True},\n    'header': {'template': 'blue', 'title': {'tag': 'plain_text', 'content': '🧪 kv_block 测试'}},\n    'elements': [kv_block(items)],\n}\npayload2 = {'receive_id': chat_id, 'msg_type': 'interactive', 'content': json.dumps(card2, ensure_ascii=False)}\nr2 = requests.post(url,\n    headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'},\n    data=json.dumps(payload2, ensure_ascii=False), timeout=10, proxies=None)\nprint(f'kv_block test: code={r2.json().get(\\\"code\\\")}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":82,"output":3486,"cacheRead":56192,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":59760,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopR